From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Karl Godard <karl@minimal.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:22:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/vsock: refuse a stream whose unix proxy cannot be
 created

When the guest opens a stream to a vsock port mapped to a host unix
socket with krun_add_vsock_port2(..., listen=false), process_op_request()
creates the host leg with UnixProxy::new(...).unwrap(). UnixProxy::new()
fails only when socket(AF_UNIX) fails (EMFILE, ENFILE, ENOBUFS, ENOMEM),
a transient host condition, but the unwrap() turns it into a panic on the
event-manager thread, and the panic aborts the whole VMM: every guest
connection and the guest itself go down because one host socket could
not be created.

Refuse just that connection instead. Log the error, which carries the
errno, and answer the guest with OP_RST, the same reply the function
already sends when a guest connects to a port that is mapped for
listening. Nothing is inserted into the proxy map, so there is no state
to clean up, and the guest's connect() fails with ECONNRESET while the
VM keeps running.

The TSI stream and dgram proxy creation paths already handle this error;
this was the only guest-triggered proxy construction that unwrapped it.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: opus-5.5
---
 src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs b/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs
index 6cf8b6f..4cc56fd 100644
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/vsock/muxer.rs
@@ -560,7 +560,7 @@ impl VsockMuxer {
                 }
                 let rxq = self.rxq.clone();
 
-                let mut unix = UnixProxy::new(
+                let mut unix = match UnixProxy::new(
                     id,
                     self.cid,
                     pkt.dst_port(),
@@ -569,8 +569,24 @@ impl VsockMuxer {
                     queue.clone(),
                     rxq,
                     path.to_path_buf(),
-                )
-                .unwrap();
+                ) {
+                    Ok(unix) => unix,
+                    Err(e) => {
+                        // Creating the host socket can fail transiently (e.g.
+                        // EMFILE, ENFILE, ENOBUFS). Refuse this connection
+                        // instead of taking the whole VM down.
+                        error!(
+                            "error creating unix proxy for port {}, sending rst: {e}",
+                            pkt.dst_port()
+                        );
+                        let rx = MuxerRx::Reset {
+                            local_port: pkt.dst_port(),
+                            peer_port: pkt.src_port(),
+                        };
+                        push_packet(self.cid, rx, &self.rxq, queue, mem);
+                        return;
+                    }
+                };
                 let tsi = TsiConnectReq {
                     peer_port: 0,
                     addr: SocketAddrV4::new(Ipv4Addr::new(0, 0, 0, 0), 0).into(),
-- 
